Result:
The Dockerized Oxia real-service script passed. JUnit XML reports
`TargetQuotaGrantStoreTest.realOxiaOwnerTakeoverReopensTargetRootAndCompletesCloseGc`: 1 test,
0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.

The regression acquires the replacement lease in ACQUIRING, rejects the stale old Owner read without a Store write,
reopens the real RocksDB Target root under a guarded read for the exact current ACQUIRING lease, then calls
`TargetWorkerOwnerActivation.activate`. It verifies the persisted Owner epoch, ACTIVE lease, and exact retry using
the original ACQUIRING lease before composing the source runtime and Worker; bounded Close GC then completes.
The lease backend and Store are real services; assignment, SourcePosition, Control registration, and source consumer
are test fixtures. This does not verify Kafka/Pulsar source fencing, production assignment/Start/Commit providers,
or application Host bootstrap. Other optional real-service smoke tests in the script were skipped because their
separate service inputs were not configured.
